From ac00e35d5dda16dc5e96baafd0b27b5b74edc350 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: a1ex <12754559+a1ex4@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:37:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] UI SIZE: larger menus and overlays on small screens

ui.h: UiScale() (the factor, to multiply a size that follows the screen by), UiLarge() (above 1,
for a layout that has to change, not only grow) and UiMinPx() (no writing under 13 pixels with
larger menus), for later pieces to use.
- The launcher, above 1x on a screen that is not a phone's: the phone's layouts (made for short
  screens) at its own unit, at most 1.5x, with the buttons' hints; the sidebar pages' previews a
  share of the page; About: the licences on two lines, the credits one a row, no QR codes where
  they do not fit.
- The pause menu's settings panel fills the screen, with narrower controls and larger names;
  the description stops above the tip; dialogs, the status bar, the party HUD, the companion
  window and its map, the key prompt and the RUN label scale with it; the pause tiles' names
  are sized a pixel at a time.
